The goal: get paid in bursts, bleed in paper cuts, and do nothing in between. Most of my trading is waiting.

This is just one style; others get paid too. This works best for me. High Sharpe, low number of trades, high quality of life where the flat periods provide rest/clarity. https://t.co/NTPG1tmNSG

being on the right side of every local move isn't realistic, certainly not with a low frequency of trading.

Impatience and emotion kills, especially when trading with leverage. Bar for taking a trade ought to be quite high.

for me that part is easy, but I've always erred on the side of undertrading and sizing conservatively-ish. There is a clear tradeoff here where you're sacrificing upside in exchange for lower downside/blowup risk and higher quality of life/avoidance of excessive stress. I never even used **any leverage** until late 2021 when I was confident we were nearing the end of a bubble and needed shorts/hedges

